<title>ITALY: Italian April wage inflation 4.5 pct. [CORRECTED 8:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>Italian April wage inflation 4.5 pct. [CORRECTED 8:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian wage inflation stood at an annual 4.5 percent in April, statistics institute ISTAT said in a statement.</p>
<p> ITALY HOURLY WAGE INFLATION   April 97    March 97</p>
<p> Year/year change		    +4.5%	+4.5%</p>
<p> Month/month change		  +0.1%	+0.1%</p>
<p> Index (base 1995=100)	    106.0	105.9</p>
<p>(Corrects index for April 97 to 106.0 from 106.1.)</p>
<p>Istat said wage inflation in the agriculture sector rose 1.3 percent year-on-year in April, 4.0 percent in the industrial sector, 2.5 percent in the chemical sector, 4.6 percent in the metalworkers sector, 3.3 percent in the service sector, 1.5 percent in the transport and communications sector and 7.2 percent in the public administration.</p>
<p>Istat added that the number of hours lost to industrial action in January, February and March was a provisional 4.2 million against 1.3 million hours in the same three months of 1996. The rise mainly reflected disputes in the manufacturing, transport and telecommunications sectors, Istat said.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
